by AmishIndy\
sethamosjones@gmail.com\
\
\
The Allard J2x was a mighty beast in its day.  In the early 1950's few cars could keep up with it on a long straightaway.  It was originally shipped to the US from england without engines because there were so many wonderful American V8s to choose from.  In the future, variants with different engines will be offered.  In this version I am working on perfecting a 331 Hemi powered version.  In its time it was the largest, most powerful engine available in the US.  Commonly in england an L head Mercury engine was fitted, and again in the states a cadillac engine was often fitted (those were famously known as Cad-Allards).    Keep a look out.  I will continue to update this as I go.\
